      "id": "figure-1",
      "filename": "figure-1-depth-reliability.svg",
      "title": "Depth breaks the constant-hop reliability model",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Required tool depth exposes a non-constant reliability process. Across 500 seeded trials at each depth, the measured curve first excludes naive p\u2081\u207f at hop 3 (0.818, 95% CI 0.781797\u20130.849354, versus 0.91833); at hop 8 it is 0.288 versus 0.796765. The result is specific to the configured decay simulator, and intervals widen at deep hops as fewer runs reach later steps.",
