      "id": "figure-4",
      "filename": "figure-4-fallback-quality.svg",
      "title": "Fallback closes the availability gap, not the quality gap",
      "caption": "Figure 4. Across 120 paired requests with 40 scheduled primary outages, fallback raised availability from 0.6667 to 1.0 while strict quality among answered requests fell from 1.0 to 0.75. Of the 40 fallback answers, 30 were silently degraded. The advisory detector recalled 0.6667 of degraded fallback answers and missed all 10 borderline-token cases, so it was not used for core success scoring.",
